title Caravan withdraw -- a phase still waiting may leave a run, on the mirror of the three facts an arrival owed
prompt Kyri lap under the autonomous loop -- read the voice and Radiant Style first, then REMEMBER, the itineraries, and the newest log recommends; close open agent-closable reds first; take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first; send each finished increment as its own signed round.
think Standfast first. Every living row in crux/REDS.md carries a closure note proven on metal -- 80, 81, 82, 83, 84, 85 (reopened and reclosed 20260819.134229), 86, 87. No agent-closable red stands open, so the line is clear for constructive work.
think The running thread is unambiguous. The newest three logs are the Caravan arc, and each recommend line names the next crux the rung before it left open. The 20260819.204716 enlist log names its own mirror outright -- a phase may now join a run under way, and nothing may yet leave one -- so the crux is a withdrawal, and the question is what a withdrawal owes the plan the way an arrival owed it three facts.
think The rota doc for this lap is foundations/20260703-182612_sameness-is-the-macro.md, and it landed exactly on the design question. Compress by making things publicly similar rather than by inventing a new mechanism. That framing is what made the finding reachable: do not invent a withdrawal reading, mirror the arrival reading.
think Reading arrive.rye's stand() and arrival_admits() showed three facts -- nobody placed waits on the newcomer's turn, its step is the next its turn has open, and a turn already standing agrees about what it follows. Each has an exact mirror. The phase still waits (so it handed out no slot, line, or grant). Its step is the last one its turn holds (so no sibling's fence falls open early). No phase in the record names its turn (so no follower is released by a predecessor that never ran).
think The deeper reason those are the right three: meet all three and every downstream reading -- elder_waits, sibling_waits, may_pass -- answers exactly what it would have answered had the phase never been written. The three facts are precisely what make a departure invisible, which is why the same walk that admits an arrival can license a departure.
think A departure must move nothing, so the run marks the phase gone where it stands rather than compacting the record. taken and gone are kept apart on purpose: one names work that ran and is judged at the end, the other names work that never will and is not. The closing accounting became finished + released == held rather than finished == held.
obs The shy reading is the measurement this rung exists to make. A supervisor asking only whether a phase still waits lets turn 4 leave while turn 5 names it, and turn 5 then starts with elder_waits reading zero -- satisfied by a turn that never came home, with nothing anywhere to report it. Measured in the pure room rather than asserted: the follower's own wait reads satisfied after the shy release.
obs The metal corrected the schedule, and that correction is worth keeping in the prose. The first draft withdrew turns 5 and 6, which the passes over the blocked head had already started; the run refused with WithdrawalStarted rather than pretending. The lawful departures are the client_a peeks queued behind the busy head, which cannot have started while turn 0 held that domain.
obs Three named errors rather than one, because a departure fails in three ways an operator must tell apart -- WithdrawalMissing, WithdrawalStarted, WithdrawalUnseated. The enlist rung proudly added no new name; here the refusals are genuinely distinct acts, so clear beats terse.
obs Withdrawal inverts arrival exactly, which is this arc's standing generalization test one tier further out. An empty turn mask was the sibling mask; a seated plan arranged to itself; a plan grown one arrival at a time was the plan its author wrote; and now a plan relieved of its own arrival is that plan, all 6 phases.
obs Both RED paths proven on metal before any GREEN claim. Dropping the named check reds the pure read in the happy zone before a child starts. Dropping the waiting check fires the module's own invariant at caravan/withdraw.rye:624 with children in flight -- the contract is load-bearing rather than decorative.
obs Thirty-eight green-witnessed Rye rings now carry the Microkit shape across real processes. TAME surface GREEN -- style bans clean, width-check exit 0 -- and the neighbor rung re-GREEN: caravan_enlist_witness passed unchanged beside the new one.
obs The limit is named in the module banner, the README, and the witness header alike: a withdrawal reaches only work still waiting. Whether a run may replace a phase -- withdraw one and enlist another in one act, so a plan may be corrected rather than only grown and pruned -- belongs to the vision room until a witness binds it.
loom witness=caravan_withdraw_witness rings=38 withdraw_tests=16 seating_tests=256 record=7 departures=2 children_pruned=5 children_whole=7 out_of_precede=0 red_paths=2
file caravan/withdraw.rye the rung -- the three-fact mirror reading, the record that may shrink while it runs, and the inverse test against arrive
file tools/caravan_withdraw_witness.rish the witness on metal -- native contains checks, the measured costs, and both RED paths named
file caravan/README.md the durable record of the rung, and the enlist section's open limit repointed now that a witness binds it
file crux/REMEMBER.md the live edge and git nib moved to this rung
recommend keep-going the honest next crux is the one this rung named its own limit -- a run may now grow and prune, yet a plan can only be corrected by doing both in sequence, which briefly leaves the record holding neither the old phase nor the new; the question becomes whether a run may replace a phase in one act, so that the three facts an arrival owes and the three a withdrawal owes are weighed together against a single record rather than one after the other.
